course: dictionary
lesson: 12245
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Constable is one of them. To find the right meaning, read the words around it, because they are its context and they leave clues. «The constable stopped the car on the high street.» The clues stopped the car and high street tell you a constable is a police officer.
explain: Capital letters can be a clue too. «John Constable painted fields and skies in the countryside.» John is a person's name, so Constable is a name here, not a job. Always ask: which meaning fits this sentence?
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. «The constable stood guard at the castle gate while the lord was away.» In a medieval castle, the constable was in charge when the lord was away, so this meaning fits. If your meaning does not make sense, try another one.
fact: Constable is a noun. You can write one constable or many constables.
fact: In the UK, Ireland, Australia, New Zealand and Canada, a constable is a police officer of the lowest rank. It is often written as PC.
fact: In history, a constable was an important officer in a medieval castle or a royal court, such as the Constable of the Tower of London.
fact: In some small towns in the United States, a constable is a local law officer.
fact: John Constable was an English painter famous for landscapes, such as «The Hay Wain» (1821).
exercise: «The constable checked the car for safety.» What does constable mean here? | A castle lord | A shop helper | A painter of pictures | *A police officer
exercise: «The constable visited our school to talk about road safety.» Who is the constable in this sentence? | A school cook | A castle guard from long ago | *A police officer who came to talk about road safety | A famous painter
exercise: «John Constable painted fields and skies in the countryside.» Find and copy the word that is the painter's surname. | fields | John | painted | *Constable
test: «In the castle, the constable was in charge when the lord was away.» What job did the constable have? | A rower on the river | A painter of hay wains | *An officer in charge of a castle | A baker in the village
test: «The constable gave the lost boy a ride home.» Which meaning fits best? | A lord of a castle | A famous painter | *A police officer | A teacher of art
exam: Sam sees «Constable» with a capital C in «Constable's Hay Wain». What is it? | A small town shop | *A painter's name | A castle officer | A police officer
